    "title": "Multi-Algorithmic Architecture for Advanced Performance Achievement in Handheld Transcoder for H.263 Wireless Communication",
    "subtitle": "[2003 G�� 2005], Designation = Research Assistant",
    "duration": "[2003 G�� 2005], Designation = Research Assistant",
    "supported": "This research was supported by the MIC (Ministry of Information and Communication), Korea, under the ITRC (Information Technology Research Center) support program supervised by the IITA (Institute of Information Technology Assessment).",
    "description": "This paper presents different issue of video streaming algorithms without compromising the video quality in the distributed environment. Our theme of this research is to manage the critical processing stages (speed, information loss, redundancy, error resilience) having better encoded ratio, without the fluctuation of quantization scale by using IP configuration. In this paper, different techniques such as upgraded features of the MC-DCT domain criteria regarded with prediction error and motion vector at low-frequency coefficient, while control of frame resolution having downscale of future prediction error with lower transmission bitrate are implemented in this streaming media. However, delay of bits in encoded buffer side is being controlled to produce the video with high quality and maintenance a low buffering delay. Our implemented results show the performance accuracy gain with better achievement than a number of previous approaches in all the above processes in an encouraging mode.",
